# This corpus is byte-exact. Its SHA-256 values are the PC-02 ground-truth oracle and
# every seeded quotation is anchored at a character offset into the extracted page text,
# so any end-of-line translation on checkout would corrupt every fixture, every offset
# and every recorded digest at once - silently, on the machine that did the checkout and
# nowhere else.
#
# This is not hypothetical. Session A4 found that a page of white scanlines has no NUL
# byte in its first 8000, so Git's content heuristic reads such a PDF as *text*. Marking
# the artefacts binary stops Git rewriting a byte and stops it trying to diff one.
#
# It also settles a smaller nuisance: a PDF cross-reference entry is required by the
# format to be exactly twenty bytes ending in a space, so `git diff --check` reports
# "trailing whitespace" on any PDF it mistakes for text. Those spaces are mandated, not
# stray.
*.pdf binary
